# Local extensions/state under .pid/ stay local — EXCEPT this project's own
# committed dogfood pid-app (.pid/index.html) and fleet recipes
# (.pid/fleet.json), which the dashboard renders/lists when pi-browser-dashboard
# is opened as a project (see the pid-apps and fleet-recipes features in
# AGENTS.md). Local `.pid/extensions/` and everything else stays ignored.
#
# Every `.pid/` at any depth, not just the repo root's. A slash inside a pattern
# anchors it, so the previous `.pid/*` covered ONLY the root — and `bun run dev`
# starts the daemon with cwd `apps/daemon`, where it writes its own
# `.pid/extensions-state.json`. That left a runtime artifact both untracked and
# LINTED: biome sets `vcs.useIgnoreFile`, so an unignored generated file failed
# `lint:ci`, and every developer running the dev daemon got a red `bun run
# verify` from a file they never wrote. Ignore all of them, then carve the root
# back out — a re-include cannot resurrect a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, hence `!/.pid/` before the root's own rules.
**/.pid/
!/.pid/
/.pid/*
!/.pid/index.html
!/.pid/fleet.json
.fallow/

# Stale Lefthook stubs — hooks install to .git/hooks (see lefthook.yml, #136)
.githooks/

# apps/cli's bundled apps/web build (bun run build:cli) — generated, not committed.
apps/cli/dist-web/

# Build artifacts regenerated on every run — tsc's incremental cache and the
# temp config Vite writes next to vite.config.ts while it loads it.
*.tsbuildinfo
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*.mjs

# Eval run output: one JSON grid per run plus each agent's raw transcript. Local
# measurements, not source — and biome sets `vcs.useIgnoreFile`, so leaving a
# generated JSON blob untracked-but-unignored would fail `lint:ci` for whoever
# ran the grid last (the same trap the .pid/ block above describes).
evals/results/

# Demo-capture scratch: the rig lives in doc/demo/README.md, not as source.
# Committing it here would put it in front of biome and fallow's dead-code scan.
.demo-tmp/
